      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# NYC Rental Listing Scores"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "5f9d7415",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Jacob Waxman"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "fcb9df82",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#### **Overview**:\n",
        "The objective of this project is to identify mispriced NYC rental apartments on Street Easy.\n",
        "\n",
        "The process is:\n",
        "1. Pull NYC apartment listings from Street Easy. The listings inlcude many different types of data, including:\n",
        "    - Images of the apartment & building\n",
        "    - Quantitative values: # of bedrooms, bathrooms, sq feet, and price\n",
        "    - Categorical values: neighborhood and available amentities\n",
        "2. Provide the images to an LLM (Gemini) via API to get a structured, quantitative metrics\n",
        "    - Up to 20 images scored per listing (unit & building pictures)\n",
        "    - Eeach image received its own result metrics which were then aggregated at the listing level\n",
        "    - More info on this at the end\n",
        "3. Test different feature components and regression models to get best results\n",
        "\n",
        "Steps 1 and 2 were done seperately. Step 3 is below:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 2,
      "id": "a63fcadc",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "from sklearn.linear_model import RidgeCV, LassoCV\n",
        "from sklearn.model_selection import (\n",
        "    GroupShuffleSplit, GroupKFold, cross_val_score,\n",
        ")\n",
        "from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\n",
        "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
        "from sklearn.metrics import r2_score, mean_absolute_error\n",
        "from sklearn.model_selection import cross_val_predict\n",
        "import sqlite3\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "from features import prepare_features, collapse_amenity_tiers, collapse_image_scores"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "5440cadf",
      "metadata": {},
